<h3>CHAPTER 4: Diffusion-Weighted Imaging (DWI) & Functional MR Applications</h3>

<p>Diffusion-Weighted Imaging measures microscopic Brownian motion of water molecules within cellular tissue, providing crucial diagnostic information within minutes of acute cellular injury.</p>

<h4>4.1 DWI, ADC & Ischemic Stroke Interpretation</h4>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Acute Ischemia Mechanism:</strong> Cytotoxic edema causes water molecules to shift into intracellular spaces, restricting diffusion.</li>
  <li><strong>b-value Selection:</strong> Higher b-values (e.g., b1000) increase diffusion weighting while suppressing normal tissue signal.</li>
  <li><strong>ADC (Apparent Diffusion Coefficient) Map:</strong> Essential to differentiate true diffusion restriction from "T2 shine-through". True acute stroke displays hyperintensity on DWI (b1000) with corresponding hypointensity (darkness) on the ADC map.</li>
</ul>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Clinical Finding</th>
      <th>DWI (b1000) Signal</th>
      <th>ADC Map Signal</th>
      <th>Clinical Diagnosis</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Acute Ischemic Stroke (&lt;6 hours)</strong></td>
      <td>Hyperintense (Bright)</td>
      <td>Hypointense (Dark)</td>
      <td>True Restricted Diffusion</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Chronic Stroke / Old Infarct</strong></td>
      <td>Hypointense / Variable</td>
      <td>Hyperintense (Bright)</td>
      <td>Facilitated Diffusion (Encephalomalacia)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>T2 Shine-Through Artifact</strong></td>
      <td>Hyperintense (Bright)</td>
      <td>Isointense / Bright</td>
      <td>No Restricted Diffusion</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Pyogenic Brain Abscess</strong></td>
      <td>Hyperintense (Bright Center)</td>
      <td>Hypointense (Dark Center)</td>
      <td>Restricted Diffusion (Viscous Pus)</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<div class="illustration-box">
  <strong>[Illustration 4.1 Placement & Prompt]</strong><br/>
  <em>Description: Axial MRI comparison showing acute ischemic stroke restricted diffusion pattern on DWI (b1000) vs. ADC Map.</em><br/>
  <strong>AI Prompt:</strong> <code>Side-by-side axial brain MRI showing acute ischemic stroke with bright signal on DWI b1000 and corresponding dark signal drop on ADC map, dark navy framing with cyan highlights, 8k --ar 16:9</code>
</div>

