<h3>CHAPTER 5: MRI Artifact Mitigation & Complete Zone Safety Protocols</h3>

<h4>5.1 Common MRI Artifacts & Solutions</h4>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Chemical Shift Artifact:</strong> Spatial misregistration along frequency encoding axis due to ~3.5 ppm Larmor frequency difference between fat and water. <em>Mitigation:</em> Increase receiver bandwidth or apply fat saturation.</li>
  <li><strong>Aliasing / Wrap-Around Artifact:</strong> Occurs when anatomical FOV exceeds selected scan limits, causing tissue outside FOV to wrap into opposite side. <em>Mitigation:</em> Increase FOV or enable Phase Oversampling (No Phase Wrap).</li>
  <li><strong>Susceptibility Artifact:</strong> Local magnetic field distortions from metallic hardware or petrous bone boundaries. <em>Mitigation:</em> Use Spin Echo over Gradient Echo, increase bandwidth, use high-order shimming.</li>
</ul>

<h4>5.2 Four-Zone MRI Safety Model</h4>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Zone Designation</th>
      <th>Access Level</th>
      <th>Operational & Safety Controls</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Zone I</strong></td>
      <td>Unrestricted General Public</td>
      <td>Hallways, waiting rooms outside MRI suite.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Zone II</strong></td>
      <td>Controlled Public Area</td>
      <td>Patient reception, dressing rooms, screening questionnaire completion.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Zone III</strong></td>
      <td>Restricted Personnel Only</td>
      <td>Control room and console area. Physical locks or badge access required. Screening mandatory.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Zone IV</strong></td>
      <td>Strictly Controlled Magnet Room</td>
      <td>Scanner room containing B0 magnet. Ferromagnetic objects strictly prohibited! Continuous 24/7 static magnetic field.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h4>5.3 MRI Technologist Safety Checklist</h4>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Safety Verification Step</th>
      <th>Required Parameter / Criterion</th>
      <th>Status</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Implant / Device Verification</td>
      <td>Confirm MR Safe / MR Conditional status for pacemakers, aneurysm clips, or neurostimulators.</td>
      <td>[  ] Pass</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Patient Metal Screening</td>
      <td>Ferromagnetic wand/detector check; remove all external metallic objects, jewelry, and clothing fasteners.</td>
      <td>[  ] Pass</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Pregnancy & Contrast Status</td>
      <td>Rule out pregnancy if Gadavist/Dotarem contrast planned; evaluate eGFR (&gt;30 mL/min for NSF prevention).</td>
      <td>[  ] Pass</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Hearing & Thermal Protection</td>
      <td>Provide earplugs / headphones (min 20 dB noise reduction); prevent skin-to-skin or cable loops to prevent RF burns.</td>
      <td>[  ] Pass</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>SAR & System Monitor</td>
      <td>Ensure Specific Absorption Rate (SAR) stays within normal operating limits (&lt;2 W/kg whole body).</td>
      <td>[  ] Pass</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

